  "markscheme": {
    "html": "<section class=\"markscheme-part\" data-label=\"14a(i)\"><p><strong>14a(i)</strong></p><p></p>\n<p>Maximum value occurs when <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"cos (\\theta) =1\"></span></p>\n<p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\Phi = 7.7 \\times (225 \\times 10^{-4}) \\approx 0.17\"></span> Wb</p>\n<p>Answer must be given to 2 s. f. in order to earn final mark.</p>\n<p></p></section><section class=\"markscheme-part\" data-label=\"14a(ii)\"><p><strong>14a(ii)</strong></p><p></p>\n<p>Since the angular speed is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{\\pi}{2}\"></span> s<span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"^{-1}\"></span>, the period of rotation is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"4\"></span> s.</p>\n<p>At <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"t = 5.5\"></span> s <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\theta = 135^{o}\"></span></p>\n<p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\Phi = 7.7 \\times (225 \\times 10^{-4}) \\times cos(135^{o}) \\approx -0.12\"></span> Wb</p>\n<p>So the magnitude of the magnetic flux is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"0.12\"></span> Wb</p>\n<p></p></section><section class=\"markscheme-part\" data-label=\"14b\"><p><strong>14b</strong></p><p></p>\n<p>Maximum value of induced emf:</p>\n<p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\varepsilon = -50 \\times \\frac{-0.17}{1} \\approx 8.5\"></span> V</p>\n<p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"(\\Delta t = 1\"></span> s since the period of rotation is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"4\"></span> s)</p>\n<p>This means that the minimum value of the induced emf is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"-8.5\"></span> V</p>\n<p>Therefore the difference is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"17\"></span> V</p>\n<p></p></section><section class=\"markscheme-part\" data-label=\"14c(i)\"><p><strong>14c(i)</strong></p><p></p>\n<p></p>\n<p>\n<figure data-asset-id=\"fig_06\"><img alt=\"Source markscheme diagram 6\" src=\"asset:fig_06\"/></figure>\n</p>\n<p></p></section><section class=\"markscheme-part\" data-label=\"14c(ii)\"><p><strong>14c(ii)</strong></p><p></p>\n<p></p>\n<p>\n<figure data-asset-id=\"fig_07\"><img alt=\"Source markscheme diagram 7\" src=\"asset:fig_07\"/></figure>\n</p>\n<p></p></section><section class=\"markscheme-part\" data-label=\"14c(iii)\"><p><strong>14c(iii)</strong></p><p> </p>\n<p>\n<figure data-asset-id=\"fig_08\"><img alt=\"Source markscheme diagram 8\" src=\"asset:fig_08\"/></figure>\n</p>\n<p></p></section>"
  },
  "paper": "paper_2",
  "question": {
    "html": "<p>A coil is rotated in a uniform magnetic field as shown on the diagram. </p>\n\n<figure data-asset-id=\"fig_01\"><img alt=\"Source question diagram 1\" src=\"asset:fig_01\"/></figure>\n\n<p>The direction of the magnetic field is vertically downwards and the coil’s axis of rotation is horizontal. The angular speed of the coil is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{\\pi}{2}\"></span> s<span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"^{-1}\"></span>, the area of the coil is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"225\"></span> cm<span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"^{2}\"></span> and the magnitude of the magnetic field strength is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"7.7\"></span> T. </p>\n<p></p>\n<p>a. At <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"t = 0\"></span> the plane of the coil is horizontal. </p>\n<p>i. Find the maximum value of the magnitude of the magnetic flux in the coil. Give your answer to an appropriate number of significant figures.</p>\n<p>  [2]</p>\n<p>ii. Calculate the magnitude of the magnetic flux in the coil at <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"t = 5.5\"></span> s.</p>\n<p>  [2]</p>\n<p>b. The coil has <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"50\"></span> turns. Calculate the <strong>difference</strong> between the maximum and minimum values of the induced emf in the coil.</p>\n<p>  [3]</p>\n<p>c. The coil is connected in series with a lightbulb. The graph shows how the induced emf in the coil varies with time. The period of rotation of the coil is T.</p>\n\n<figure data-asset-id=\"fig_02\"><img alt=\"Source question diagram 2\" src=\"asset:fig_02\"/></figure>\n\n<p>Sketch on the diagram:</p>\n<p>i. how the flux linkage in the coil varies with time.</p>\n\n<figure data-asset-id=\"fig_03\"><img alt=\"Source question diagram 3\" src=\"asset:fig_03\"/></figure>\n\n<p>  [2]</p>\n<p>ii. how the power dissipated in the lightbulb varies with time.</p>\n\n<figure data-asset-id=\"fig_04\"><img alt=\"Source question diagram 4\" src=\"asset:fig_04\"/></figure>\n\n<p>  [2]</p>\n<p>iii. how the induced emf in the coil varies with time when the speed of the coil’s rotation is doubled.</p>\n\n<figure data-asset-id=\"fig_05\"><img alt=\"Source question diagram 5\" src=\"asset:fig_05\"/></figure>\n\n<p> [2]</p>"
  },
